{"id": "EUVD-2026-86043", "enisaUuid": "3f28adbb-403b-35db-94ed-7ef5936846c0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxhci: Prevent queuing new commands if xhci is inaccessible\n\nRefuse to queue a new command on the command ring if xHC is marked\ninaccessible with the HCD_FLAG_HW_ACCESSIBLE.\n\nHCD_FLAG_HW_ACCESSIBLE is set and cleared in suspend and resume.\n\nAlso print a warning if xhci is being suspended with commands\nstill pending on the command ring.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e2eaa000e4e5ad46b7cf8fcf1e4a2585ef8b5a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/add3aeb74e2c7d82fa1035af2a027666c6906210", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a215190ef68ca3602fe00674e0efffad71beb3aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fec259e46d44317379834a44115fae66122dc93f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a50948386256b24d73971b9a152fe1de808446ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a05e54c1eeaba10414aa2fde94589a7c9885f2a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/82b70c799281cc24506085be978b829149ba0ca4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-57g2-jm7m-f2mp", "CVE-2026-97430"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0509fb40-3ab2-35b7-a977-c5bc56b16562", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "0a754726-784a-30dd-88fa-8367e12fbfb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5535b1d5f8885695c6ded783c692e3c0d0eda8ca <a05e54c1eeaba10414aa2fde94589a7c9885f2a1"}, {"id": "0d6fb708-d1af-3639-909e-b4d3fe075308", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.37"}, {"id": "235073b7-9c76-3a07-b4b7-29e0f1bf84f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "29d746ce-6ea8-3fcf-896b-171de9e7167d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Lin